; expect 42
; A lambda of several parameters. Every lambda in this repository takes
; ONE, which is why nothing noticed that two had no representation at
; all: `checkLam` typed a multi-parameter lambda as taking a TUPLE, so
; an ordinary call was refused with a type naming something nobody
; wrote - `expected (_t0, _t1), found Int` - and the emitter, on the
; paths that got past the checker, produced no `_lam_` function and
; folded the whole application to its last argument at exit 0.
;
; It is now parsed as what the curried types already said it was:
; `(lambda (x y) b)` is `(lambda (x) (lambda (y) b))`, which the
; closure representation has always implemented - one hidden `%_env`
; per lifted body, capture by value of everything in scope, so the
; inner lambda captures `x` the way it captures any other enclosing
; binding.
;
; Five terms, each failing differently if the desugar is wrong:
;
;   (add2 20 22)      42 - two parameters, applied at once. Under the
;                          old rule this file did not compile.
;   (add3 10 15 17)   42 - three, so the nesting is not special-cased
;                          at two.
;   (withCap 5 7)     42 - the inner lambda must capture `k` from the
;                          enclosing `let`, not just the outer
;                          parameter. If capture walks only one level
;                          this is 12.
;   (partial 22)      42 - the intermediate value of a partial
;                          application IS the inner closure, which is
;                          the whole point of currying and the thing a
;                          tuple parameter cannot express.
;   (shadow 1 2)      42 - the inner parameter shadows a same-named
;                          binding outside, and the capture must not
;                          win over the parameter.
(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (let ((add2 (lambda (x y) (+ x y)))
        (add3 (lambda (x y z) (+ (+ x y) z)))
        (k 30))
    (let ((withCap (lambda (a b) (+ k (+ a b))))
          (y 100))
      (let ((shadow (lambda (p y) (+ (* p 40) (+ y 0)))))
        (let ((partial (add2 20)))
          (if (&& (&& (== (add2 20 22) 42)
                      (== (add3 10 15 17) 42))
                  (&& (== (withCap 5 7) 42)
                      (&& (== (partial 22) 42)
                          (== (shadow 1 2) 42))))
              42
              1))))))
